IMPORT prelude

-- Science Centre Act 1970 (Singapore) -- the financial year (s 2), the Board's numbers, vacancies and temporary appointments
-- (s 4), the temporary chief executive (s 7(2)), which acts need the Minister (ss 6, 13A, 14, 18, 19), delegation (s 10),
-- protection from personal liability (s 11), sealing of documents (s 12), the Science Centre Fund (ss 14, 15), and the ceiling
-- on penalties that regulations may set (s 20(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ScCA1970.txt. The deposit
-- says it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the
-- latest amending Act annotated in the text is Act 5 of 2018 (the Public Sector (Governance) Act 2018), at ss 2, 7, 8, 9, 10,
-- 16, 17, 18 and 20.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0203 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The answer the text gives is: almost nothing directly. It is a short institutional Act that
-- creates the Science Centre Board and makes it run the Science Centre. What reaches a visitor is s 6(i) (the Board regulates
-- public access and charges fees for it, with no ceiling and no approval step in the Act) and s 20(2) (regulations about the
-- Centre and its premises may create offences punishable by a fine of at most $1,000). What reaches a business dealing with
-- the Board is s 6(d) (property deals need the Minister), s 12 (how a sealed deed is proved) and s 11 (members are protected).
-- SCOPED to the rules with decision content. Not encoded: short title (s 1), incorporation (s 3), the duty to run the Centre
-- (s 5) beyond its use in s 6, the general powers in s 6(a)-(c), (f), (g), the chief executive's appointment under the Public
-- Sector (Governance) Act 2018 (s 7(1), (3)), Ministerial directions and information (s 9), grants (s 13), the Minister's
-- making of regulations (s 20(1)), and the repealed ss 8, 16, 17. No regulations made under s 20 were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Science Centre Act 1970 -- the Board`

§§ `2 -- financial year`

-- s 2: "'financial year' means a period of 12 months beginning on 1 April in any year".
-- Returned: the calendar year in which the financial year containing the given month began (months numbered 1-12).
GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the financial year began in` IS
    IF `month` >= 4 THEN `calendar year` ELSE `calendar year` - 1

§§ `4 -- constitution, vacancies and temporary appointments`

-- s 4(1): the Board consists of a Chairperson, a Deputy Chairperson "and (c) not less than 7 but not more than 15 other members",
-- all appointed by the Minister.
GIVEN `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the number of other members is within section 4(1)(c)` IF
    `number of other members` >= 7 AND `number of other members` <= 15

-- s 4(7): "The Board may act despite any vacancy in its membership."
-- So a Board below the s 4(1)(c) minimum is not thereby disabled. (The text says nothing about appointments beyond 15; that is not
-- a vacancy and is not decided here.)
GIVEN `number of other members` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a vacancy prevents the Board from acting` IF
    FALSE

-- s 4(3): the Minister may appoint "any person" to be a temporary member "during the temporary incapacity from illness or otherwise,
-- or during the temporary absence from Singapore, of any member".
GIVEN `the member is temporarily incapacitated` IS A BOOLEAN, `the member is temporarily absent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may appoint a temporary member` IF
    `the member is temporarily incapacitated` OR `the member is temporarily absent from Singapore`

-- s 4(4): the Minister may appoint "any member of the Board" to be a temporary Chairperson or temporary Deputy Chairperson during
-- the same kinds of incapacity or absence of the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson. Unlike s 4(3) ("any person"), the temporary
-- officer must already be a member.
GIVEN `the appointee is a member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officeholder is temporarily incapacitated or absent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may appoint the temporary Chairperson or Deputy` IF
    `the appointee is a member of the Board` AND `the officeholder is temporarily incapacitated or absent from Singapore`

§§ `7(2) -- temporary chief executive`

-- s 7(2): the Board may appoint an individual to act temporarily as chief executive when the chief executive "(a) is absent from
-- duty or Singapore; or (b) is, for any reason, unable to perform the duties of the office" (subject to the Public Sector
-- (Governance) Act 2018, which was not read).
GIVEN `absent from duty` IS A BOOLEAN, `absent from Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `unable to perform the duties for any reason` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may appoint an acting chief executive` IF
    `absent from duty` OR `absent from Singapore` OR `unable to perform the duties for any reason`

§§ `6, 13A, 14, 18, 19 -- what needs the Minister`

-- s 6(d): "with the approval of the Minister, to acquire, purchase, lease, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property ...
-- and sell, convey, assign, surrender ... mortgage ... or otherwise dispose of" property vested in the Board. Read here as one
-- approval governing both acquisition and disposal, since both sit in the one paragraph after the approval words.
-- s 6(e), (h), (i), (j), (k): erecting buildings, receiving donations and raising funds, "to regulate and control public access to the
-- Science Centre and charge fees for such access", training scholarships, and contracts -- no approval words.
-- s 10: committees and delegation are "in its discretion". s 14: moneys go to "any bank that may be decided by the Board" (the Fund
-- is "subject to the directions of the Minister", which is not an approval of the choice). s 19: investment under the standard
-- investment power of statutory bodies (Interpretation Act 1965 s 33A, not read).
-- s 18: estimates go to the Minister, who "may approve or disallow any item"; "the Board is bound by the Minister's decision".
-- s 13A: shares are issued to the Minister for Finance "as that Minister may direct" -- a direction, not a Board act needing approval;
-- not in the list below.
DECLARE `Board act` IS ONE OF
    `acquiring land`
    `selling or mortgaging property`
    `charging an admission fee`
    `raising an admission fee`
    `erecting a building`
    `accepting a donation`
    `offering a training scholarship`
    `entering into a contract`
    `choosing the bank for the Fund`
    `investing its moneys`
    `adopting the annual estimates`

GIVEN `the act` IS A `Board act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's approval is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the act`
    WHEN `acquiring land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `selling or mortgaging property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `adopting the annual estimates` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10 -- delegation`

-- s 10(1): committees may consist "of persons who may or may not be members of the Board".
-- s 10(2): the Board may delegate "to any committee mentioned in subsection (1) or the chairperson of that committee or any employee
-- of the Board". An individual Board member who neither chairs a committee nor is an employee is not on that list, nor is an
-- outside contractor.
DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a committee`
    `the chairperson of a committee`
    `an employee of the Board`
    `a Board member acting alone`
    `an outside contractor`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may delegate its powers to` IF
    CONSIDER `the delegate`
    WHEN `a committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the chairperson of a committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an employee of the Board` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `11 -- protection from personal liability`

-- s 11(1): "No action, suit, prosecution or proceedings shall be brought or instituted against any member of the Board in respect of
-- any act done bona fide in pursuance or execution or intended execution of this Act."
-- s 11 names members only. Whether officers and employees are protected elsewhere (for instance by the Public Sector (Governance)
-- Act 2018) was not read; this rule answers only for s 11.
GIVEN `is a member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution or intended execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 11 bars proceedings against the person` IF
    `is a member of the Board` AND `acted bona fide` AND `in execution or intended execution of the Act`

-- s 11(2): "Where any member of the Board is exempt from liability by reason only of this section, the Board itself is liable only to
-- the extent that it would be if that member of the Board were an employee or agent of the Board."
GIVEN `is a member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted bona fide` IS A BOOLEAN, `in execution or intended execution of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `exempt by reason only of section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board answers as if the member were its employee or agent` IF
    `section 11 bars proceedings against the person` `is a member of the Board` `acted bona fide` `in execution or intended execution of the Act`
    AND `exempt by reason only of section 11`

§§ `12 -- execution of documents`

-- s 12: instruments requiring the seal "must be sealed with the common seal of the Board in the presence of the Chairperson or the
-- Deputy Chairperson and one other member of the Board, who must sign every such deed ... and their signing is sufficient evidence
-- that the seal was duly and properly affixed". s 2: "Chairperson" and "Deputy Chairperson" include a temporary one.
DECLARE Sealing HAS
    `sealed with the common seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson, including a temporary one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `before one other member of the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
    `both of them signed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sealing` IS A Sealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signatures are sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the sealing`'s `sealed with the common seal`
    AND `the sealing`'s `before the Chairperson or Deputy Chairperson, including a temporary one`
    AND `the sealing`'s `before one other member of the Board`
    AND `the sealing`'s `both of them signed`

§§ `14, 15 -- the Science Centre Fund`

-- s 14: "All moneys received or raised by the Board must forthwith be paid into" a bank to the credit of the Science Centre Fund.
-- s 15: the Fund "must be devoted solely to" (a) the expenses of the administration of the Board and (b) "all expenses necessary for
-- carrying out the purposes of this Act".
DECLARE Receipt IS ONE OF
    `admission fees`
    `a private donation`
    `a Government grant`

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it must be paid into the Fund` IF
    TRUE

DECLARE Outlay IS ONE OF
    `staff salaries of the Board`
    `buying a new exhibit`
    `a gift to an unrelated charity`

GIVEN `the outlay` IS A Outlay
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Fund may pay for` IF
    CONSIDER `the outlay`
    WHEN `staff salaries of the Board` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying a new exhibit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `20(2) -- penalties in regulations`

-- s 20(2): regulations "(a) may prescribe that any act or omission in contravention of any regulation is an offence; and (b) may
-- provide for the imposition of a penalty not exceeding a fine of $1,000 for such offence". No imprisonment is mentioned.
GIVEN `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER, `provides for imprisonment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the penalty is within section 20(2)` IF
    `maximum fine` <= 1000 AND (NOT `provides for imprisonment`)
